> However I would like to know some more about this level creation. I
> have visited Valkyrie quest end levels quite a few times and this was
> the first time when the stairs were in the middle of lava. Because
> most of the level is covered with lava I don't think that the stairs
> are just randomly generated somewhere on the level. Otherwise I would
> have seen similar situations many times. How the game decides to where
> it puts the stairs?

The stairs are always in the same location: 28 squares right of
Surtur's starting spot, two rows down. What changes is whether that
spot happens to be adjacent to dry land. The way that the lava plain
gets laid out and the fact that the stairs have eight adjacent
squares, any of which will do, mean that it's _usually_ going to be
accessible; but it's far from guaranteed.

(It's also possible for the island on the right hand side to be
disconnected from the big island in the centre, but that's a good deal
rarer.)

